      'Not quite. The formula is Expected Loss = PD x LGD x EAD. Plugging in: 0.0018 x 0.60 x $50,000,000 = $54,000. The PD must be expressed as a decimal (0.18% = 0.0018), and the LGD of 60% means only 60% of the exposure is lost (40% is recovered).'
