            { label: 'Keep the tech focus, it\'s been profitable and the relationships are strong', consequence: 'SVB had the strongest tech banking relationships in the industry, and they meant nothing when fear set in. Peter Thiel\'s Founders Fund, a longtime SVB client, was among the first to tell portfolio companies to withdraw. Relationships don\'t prevent bank runs; liquidity buffers and diversification do.', score: 0 },
            { label: 'Increase FDIC insurance marketing to encourage depositors to stay below $250K limits', consequence: 'Tech startups keep millions in operating cash, they need large uninsured deposits for payroll and operations. Asking them to split into $250K chunks across dozens of banks is impractical. The solution must address institutional deposits as they actually exist, not as you wish they were.', score: 1 }
