            { label: 'Trust the current correlations, a year of data is sufficient', consequence: 'LTCM had four years of near-zero correlations before everything moved together in 1998. One year of data tells you about normal markets, not crisis markets. The correlations you need to worry about are the ones you\'ve never seen, the regime-change correlations that emerge during panic.', score: 0 },
            { label: 'Diversify into more strategies to drive correlations even lower', consequence: 'Adding strategies reduces normal-market correlation but does nothing for crisis correlation. During panics, even "uncorrelated" assets like real estate, commodities, and emerging market bonds can move together as forced selling hits every asset class. More diversification without correlation stress testing is a false comfort.', score: 1 }
