      'Options and hedging are the most powerful tools in risk management, but they are tools, not magic. LTCM had the best mathematical models ever created and still lost $4.6 billion because they ignored leverage limits, liquidity risk, and correlation breakdown. Goldman Sachs used simpler strategies with disciplined execution and survived the worst crisis in 80 years. The lesson: hedging discipline beats hedging sophistication every time. Buy protection when it\'s cheap, keep leverage manageable, and always stress test for the scenario your models say is "impossible."'
