        { term: 'Duration Matching', definition: 'An investment strategy where the duration of assets is matched to the duration of liabilities, immunizing the portfolio against interest rate changes.', example: 'A pension fund owing benefits with a 15-year duration invests in bonds with 15-year duration so that rate changes affect assets and liabilities equally.' }
