            { label: 'Let each division keep its own model, they know their businesses best', consequence: 'This is the pre-London Whale JPMorgan approach. When each division uses different models, you can\'t aggregate risk across the firm. You have no enterprise-wide view. Concentrated exposures hide in the gaps between silos.', score: 0 },
            { label: 'Force a single model on everyone and tell the IB head to deal with it', consequence: 'The IB head has a legitimate point, exotic derivatives genuinely require more sophisticated models than simple loans. A one-size-fits-all approach sacrifices accuracy. The answer is standardized reporting WITH supplemental models, not standardization that ignores product complexity.', score: 1 }
