            { label: 'Inform the division heads and ask them to coordinate between themselves', consequence: 'Coordination without mandated limits is wishful thinking. Credit Suisse\'s divisions knew about Archegos independently but no one owned the enterprise view. ERM must enforce firm-wide limits, not rely on voluntary coordination between divisions competing for revenue.', score: 1 },
            { label: 'Monitor the situation but don\'t act, 18% is manageable', consequence: 'This is exactly how concentration risk builds unchecked. Archegos was "manageable" at Credit Suisse until it wasn\'t. An 18% capital exposure to a single counterparty is a potential firm-killer. ERM exists to act on these findings, not just observe them.', score: 0 }
